# November 20, 2026: downtown, South Troy and the east side of Troy, region troy (Troy & Lansingburgh), drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny. Five of the thin lm- landmark pins round Monument Square and the Burden office get full
# entries (was=), and the rest are standing buildings and marked sites the Atlas lacked: the 1904 commercial buildings on
# Monument Square, the 1936 post office with its Waldo Peirce murals, two firehouses, a school, a church and three markers
# from the Uncle Sam Memorial Foundation and others.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), the Wikipedia Register list for Rensselaer
# County (--rows), HMdb marker pages, the Hudson Mohawk Industrial Gateway's museum and office-building pages, the Hart
# Cluett Museum's visit page, the Troy Savings Bank Music Hall's box-office page and historypointer.com (Register address),
# all through tools/page.py; positions from the ArcGIS geocoder (tools/geo.py) and OpenStreetMap (tools/nom.py, osmnear.py).
